    "updated_at": "2021-06-28T21:16:49Z",
    "body": "I think that this is not correct. The docs say the following:\r\n\r\n> The module will be shown only if there are background jobs running. The module will show the number > of jobs running if there is more than 1 job, or more than the threshold config value, if it exists.\r\n\r\nand the relevant bit of code in the `jobs` module is:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n    let module_number = if num_of_jobs > config.threshold || config.threshold == 0 {\r\n        num_of_jobs.to_string()\r\n    } else {\r\n        \"\".to_string()\r\n    };\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich shows that the condition for showing the job count is `if num_of_jobs > config.threshold`.",
